window.products.push({"id":96563,"name":"WP8577274 8577274 Dryer Thermistor Fuse Whirlpool 3976615 Kenmore Maytag Duet Thermal Part Thermostat AP6013514 PS11746740 Compatible GEW9200LW0 MEDB7","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":5.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61PHrrnoNeL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Whirlpool 8577274 Thermistor For Dryer - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers WP8577274, AP6013514, 1181075, 3390292, 3406294, 3976615, 772546, ER8577274, PS11746740, WP8577274VP. Dryer Part 8577274 is compatible with Whirlpool, Amana, Crosley, Inglis, Kenmore, KitchenAid, Maytag appliances. It fits hundreds of models and can be installed in minutes. Thermistor is made of premium materials to deliver precise temperature readings, promoting safe and efficient operation of the dryer. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Wp8577274 Whirlpool Thermistor? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Replacing the 8577274 Dryer Thermistor is a relatively simple process that can be done in a few minutes. Whirlpool Thermistor 8577274 will help if your appliance shuts off too soon, there's no heat or not enough heat, it doesn't start, or is too hot. 💡 Whirlpool Dryer Thermistor Wp8577274 keeps the dryer from getting too hot by constantly regulating and monitoring its temperature. It works by sensing the temperature of the dryer drum and opening or closing the circuit to the heating element as needed to maintain the desired temperature. It is located near the thermal fuse on the blower housing. Our Thermistor 8577274 meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 How do you know if a dryer thermostat is bad? There are a few signs that can indicate that a dryer thermostat is bad or faulty. Here are some common symptoms to look out for: Clothes aren't drying properly; Dryer is overheating; Dryer won't start; Dryer is shutting off too soon. It's important to diagnose any issues with the dryer thermostat promptly, as failing to do so can potentially cause harm to other parts of the system. 💡 How do you test a thermistor 8577274? Disconnect the dryer from its power source and gas supply (if applicable). Locate the thermistor on the blower housing or exhaust duct and disconnect it from the wiring harness. Measure resistance using a multimeter and compare the reading to the manufacturer's specifications. An acceptable reading is generally between 10,000 and 30,000 ohms at room temperature. Replace the thermistor if the resistance reading falls outside of the acceptable range.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61PHrrnoNeL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07YD7VDWG","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-96563","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07YD7VDWG","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07YD7VDWG","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
